{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Joseph was brought down to Egypt.</b> And before Joseph's descent, Judah went down, to fulfill the last redeemer — this is King Mashiach, who shall come from Peretz, as it is said: וירד יהודה וגו׳." "<b>Was brought down.</b> It does not say 'went down' but 'was brought down,' to fulfill the decree of the Place, to roll the matter toward bringing our forefathers down to Egypt. A parable: a cow that they wanted to bring into the slaughterhouse but she refused. What did they do? They took her calf and brought it there in front of her; she too immediately ran and entered after it. So too when Joseph was brought down, his brothers entered, to fulfill the decree of the Place, blessed be He."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:40.437318868Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}